      {
        "id": 8247,
        "name": "burningneuron",
        "username": "burningneuron",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/burningneuron/{size}/2653_2.png",
        "created_at": "2013-06-20T14:17:59.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>Ra's card comes into play that says all hero damage is fire, and all fire damage is +1.</p><p>Pike Industrial's card comes into play that says all damage is toxic, all damage +1.</p><p>Resolving them in play order, do we:</p><p>A) hero does 2 whatever damage, Ra converts it to fire and gives it +1, then PI turns it toxic and gives it an additional +1 for 4 damage, or...</p><p>B) hero does 2 damage, Ra converts it to fire, it gets +1 for being fire but then loses the +1 when PI turns it to toxic, then gets +1 for the PI card's global modifier, for 3 damage?</p><p>I'm not married to either answer, both seem right, but my gut says B. &nbsp;What says the group?</p>",
        "post_number": 1,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T01:38:43.404Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
        "reply_to_post_number": null,
        "quote_count": 0,
        "incoming_link_count": 4,
        "reads": 0,
        "readers_count": 0,
        "score": 20.0,
        "yours": false,
        "topic_id": 8245,
        "topic_slug": "stacking-static-modifiers",
        "display_username": "burningneuron",
        "primary_group_name": null,
